@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.2089 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [13290 x i8] }> <{ [13290 x i8] c"# `asm_experimental_arch`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#93335]\0A\0A[#93335]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/93335\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThis feature tracks `asm!` and `global_asm!` support for the following architectures:\0A- NVPTX\0A- PowerPC\0A- Hexagon\0A- MIPS32r2 and MIPS64r2\0A- wasm32\0A- BPF\0A- SPIR-V\0A- AVR\0A- MSP430\0A- M68k\0A- CSKY\0A- s390x\0A\0A## Register classes\0A\0A| Architecture | Register class | Registers                          | LLVM constraint code |\0A| ------------ | -------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------- |\0A| MIPS         | `reg`          | `$[2-25]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| MIPS         | `freg`         | `$f[0-31]`                         | `f`                  |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg16`        | None\\*                             | `h`                  |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg32`        | None\\*                             | `r`                  |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg64`        | None\\*                             | `l`                  |\0A| Hexagon      | `reg`          | `r[0-28]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg`          | `r[0-31]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg_nonzero`  | `r[1-31]`                          | `b`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `freg`         | `f[0-31]`                          | `f`                  |\0A| PowerPC      | `cr`           | `cr[0-7]`, `cr`                    | Only clobbers        |\0A| PowerPC      | `xer`          | `xer`                              | Only clobbers        |\0A| wasm32       | `local`        | None\\*                             | `r`                  |\0A| BPF          | `reg`          | `r[0-10]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| BPF          | `wreg`         | `w[0-10]`                          | `w`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg`          | `r[2-25]`, `XH`, `XL`, `ZH`, `ZL`  | `r`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_upper`    | `r[16-25]`, `XH`, `XL`, `ZH`, `ZL` | `d`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_pair`     | `r3r2` .. `r25r24`, `X`, `Z`       | `r`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_iw`       | `r25r24`, `X`, `Z`                 | `w`                  |\0A| AVR          | `reg_ptr`      | `X`, `Z`                           | `e`                  |\0A| MSP430       | `reg`          | `r[0-15]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| M68k         | `reg`          | `d[0-7]`, `a[0-7]`                 | `r`                  |\0A| M68k         | `reg_data`     | `d[0-7]`                           | `d`                  |\0A| M68k         | `reg_addr`     | `a[0-3]`                           | `a`                  |\0A| CSKY         | `reg`          | `r[0-31]`                          | `r`                  |\0A| CSKY         | `freg`         | `f[0-31]`                          | `f`                  |\0A| s390x        | `reg`          | `r[0-10]`, `r[12-14]`              | `r`                  |\0A| s390x        | `freg`         | `f[0-15]`                          | `f`                  |\0A\0A> **Notes**:\0A> - NVPTX doesn't have a fixed register set, so named registers are not supported.\0A>\0A> - WebAssembly doesn't have registers, so named registers are not supported.\0A\0A# Register class supported types\0A\0A| Architecture | Register class                  | Target feature | Allowed types                           |\0A| ------------ | ------------------------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------- |\0A| MIPS32       | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `f32`               |\0A| MIPS32       | `freg`                          | None           | `f32`, `f64`                            |\0A| MIPS64       | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`, `f32`, `f64` |\0A| MIPS64       | `freg`                          | None           | `f32`, `f64`                            |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg16`                         | None           | `i8`, `i16`                             |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg32`                         | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `f32`               |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg64`                         | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `f32`, `i64`, `f64` |\0A| Hexagon      | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `f32`               |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`                      |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg_nonzero`                   | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`                      |\0A| PowerPC      | `freg`                          | None           | `f32`, `f64`                            |\0A| PowerPC      | `cr`                            | N/A            | Only clobbers                           |\0A| PowerPC      | `xer`                           | N/A            | Only clobbers                           |\0A| wasm32       | `local`                         | None           | `i8` `i16` `i32` `i64` `f32` `f64`      |\0A| BPF          | `reg`                           | None           | `i8` `i16` `i32` `i64`                  |\0A| BPF          | `wreg`                          | `alu32`        | `i8` `i16` `i32`                        |\0A| AVR          | `reg`, `reg_upper`              | None           | `i8`                                    |\0A| AVR          | `reg_pair`, `reg_iw`, `reg_ptr` | None           | `i16`                                   |\0A| MSP430       | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`                             |\0A| M68k         | `reg`, `reg_addr`               | None           | `i16`, `i32`                            |\0A| M68k         | `reg_data`                      | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`                      |\0A| CSKY         | `reg`                           | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`                      |\0A| CSKY         | `freg`                          | None           | `f32`,                                  |\0A| s390x        | `reg`, `reg_addr`               | None           | `i8`, `i16`, `i32`, `i64`               |\0A| s390x        | `freg`                          | None           | `f32`, `f64`                            |\0A\0A## Register aliases\0A\0A| Architecture | Base register | Aliases   |\0A| ------------ | ------------- | --------- |\0A| Hexagon      | `r29`         | `sp`      |\0A| Hexagon      | `r30`         | `fr`      |\0A| Hexagon      | `r31`         | `lr`      |\0A| BPF          | `r[0-10]`     | `w[0-10]` |\0A| AVR          | `XH`          | `r27`     |\0A| AVR          | `XL`          | `r26`     |\0A| AVR          | `ZH`          | `r31`     |\0A| AVR          | `ZL`          | `r30`     |\0A| MSP430       | `r0`          | `pc`      |\0A| MSP430       | `r1`          | `sp`      |\0A| MSP430       | `r2`          | `sr`      |\0A| MSP430       | `r3`          | `cg`      |\0A| MSP430       | `r4`          | `fp`      |\0A| M68k         | `a5`          | `bp`      |\0A| M68k         | `a6`          | `fp`      |\0A| M68k         | `a7`          | `sp`, `usp`, `ssp`, `isp` |\0A| CSKY         | `r[0-3]`      | `a[0-3]`  |\0A| CSKY         | `r[4-11]`     | `l[0-7]`  |\0A| CSKY         | `r[12-13]`    | `t[0-1]`  |\0A| CSKY         | `r14`         | `sp`      |\0A| CSKY         | `r15`         | `lr`      |\0A| CSKY         | `r[16-17]`    | `l[8-9]`  |\0A| CSKY         | `r[18-25]`    | `t[2-9]`  |\0A| CSKY         | `r28`         | `rgb`     |\0A| CSKY         | `r29`         | `rtb`     |\0A| CSKY         | `r30`         | `svbr`    |\0A| CSKY         | `r31`         | `tls`     |\0A\0A> **Notes**:\0A> - TI does not mandate a frame pointer for MSP430, but toolchains are allowed\0A    to use one; LLVM uses `r4`.\0A\0A## Unsupported registers\0A\0A| Architecture | Unsupported register                    | Reason                                                                                                                                                                              |\0A| ------------ | --------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\0A| All          | `sp`, `r15` (s390x)                     | The stack pointer must be restored to its original value at the end of an asm code block.                                                                                           |\0A| All          | `fr` (Hexagon), `$fp` (MIPS), `Y` (AVR), `r4` (MSP430), `a6` (M68k), `r11` (s390x) | The frame pointer cannot be used as an input or output.                                                                                                                             |\0A| All          | `r19` (Hexagon)                         | This is used internally by LLVM as a \22base pointer\22 for functions with complex stack frames.                                                                                        |\0A| MIPS         | `$0` or `$zero`                         | This is a constant zero register which can't be modified.                                                                                                                           |\0A| MIPS         | `$1` or `$at`                           | Reserved for assembler.                                                                                                                                                             |\0A| MIPS         | `$26`/`$k0`, `$27`/`$k1`                | OS-reserved registers.                                                                                                                                                              |\0A| MIPS         | `$28`/`$gp`                             | Global pointer cannot be used as inputs or outputs.                                                                                                                                 |\0A| MIPS         | `$ra`                                   | Return address cannot be used as inputs or outputs.                                                                                                                                 |\0A| Hexagon      | `lr`                                    | This is the link register which cannot be used as an input or output.                                                                                                               |\0A| AVR          | `r0`, `r1`, `r1r0`                      | Due to an issue in LLVM, the `r0` and `r1` registers cannot be used as inputs or outputs.  If modified, they must be restored to their original values before the end of the block. |\0A|MSP430        | `r0`, `r2`, `r3`                        | These are the program counter, status register, and constant generator respectively. Neither the status register nor constant generator can be written to.                          |\0A| M68k         | `a4`, `a5`                              | Used internally by LLVM for the base pointer and global base pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r7`, `r28`                             | Used internally by LLVM for the base pointer and global base pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r8`                                    | Used internally by LLVM for the frame pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r14`                                   | Used internally by LLVM for the stack pointer. |\0A| CSKY         | `r15`                                   | This is the link register. |\0A| CSKY         | `r[26-30]`                              | Reserved by its ABI.       |\0A| CSKY         | `r31`                                   | This is the TLS register.  |\0A\0A\0A## Template modifiers\0A\0A| Architecture | Register class | Modifier | Example output | LLVM modifier |\0A| ------------ | -------------- | -------- | -------------- | ------------- |\0A| MIPS         | `reg`          | None     | `$2`           | None          |\0A| MIPS         | `freg`         | None     | `$f0`          | None          |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg16`        | None     | `rs0`          | None          |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg32`        | None     | `r0`           | None          |\0A| NVPTX        | `reg64`        | None     | `rd0`          | None          |\0A| Hexagon      | `reg`          | None     | `r0`           | None          |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg`          | None     | `0`            | None          |\0A| PowerPC      | `reg_nonzero`  | None     | `3`            | None          |\0A| PowerPC      | `freg`         | None     | `0`            | None          |\0A| s390x        | `reg`          | None     | `%r0`          | None          |\0A| s390x        | `reg_addr`     | None     | `%r1`          | None          |\0A| s390x        | `freg`         | None     | `%f0`          | None          |\0A| CSKY         | `reg`          | None     | `r0`           | None          |\0A| CSKY         | `freg`         | None     | `f0`           | None          |\0A\0A# Flags covered by `preserves_flags`\0A\0AThese flags registers must be restored upon exiting the asm block if the `preserves_flags` option is set:\0A- AVR\0A  - The status register `SREG`.\0A- MSP430\0A  - The status register `r2`.\0A- M68k\0A  - The condition code register `ccr`.\0A- s390x\0A  - The condition code register `cc`.\0A" }>, align 1
