@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.2450 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [784 x i8] }> <{ [784 x i8] c"# `custom_test_frameworks`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#50297]\0A\0A[#50297]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/50297\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AThe `custom_test_frameworks` feature allows the use of `#[test_case]` and `#![test_runner]`.\0AAny function, const, or static can be annotated with `#[test_case]` causing it to be aggregated (like `#[test]`)\0Aand be passed to the test runner determined by the `#![test_runner]` crate attribute.\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(custom_test_frameworks)]\0A#![test_runner(my_runner)]\0A\0Afn my_runner(tests: &[&i32]) {\0A    for t in tests {\0A        if **t == 0 {\0A            println!(\22PASSED\22);\0A        } else {\0A            println!(\22FAILED\22);\0A        }\0A    }\0A}\0A\0A#[test_case]\0Aconst WILL_PASS: i32 = 0;\0A\0A#[test_case]\0Aconst WILL_FAIL: i32 = 4;\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
