@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.3067 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [1499 x i8] }> <{ [1499 x i8] c"# `start`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is: [#29633]\0A\0A[#29633]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/29633\0A\0A------------------------\0A\0AAllows you to mark a function as the entry point of the executable, which is\0Anecessary in `#![no_std]` environments.\0A\0AThe function marked `#[start]` is passed the command line parameters in the same\0Aformat as the C main function (aside from the integer types being used).\0AIt has to be non-generic and have the following signature:\0A\0A```rust,ignore (only-for-syntax-highlight)\0A# let _:\0Afn(isize, *const *const u8) -> isize\0A# ;\0A```\0A\0AThis feature should not be confused with the `start` *lang item* which is\0Adefined by the `std` crate and is written `#[lang = \22start\22]`.\0A\0A## Usage together with the `std` crate\0A\0A`#[start]` can be used in combination with the `std` crate, in which case the\0Anormal `main` function (which would get called from the `std` crate) won't be\0Aused as an entry point.\0AThe initialization code in `std` will be skipped this way.\0A\0AExample:\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(start)]\0A\0A#[start]\0Afn start(_argc: isize, _argv: *const *const u8) -> isize {\0A    0\0A}\0A```\0A\0AUnwinding the stack past the `#[start]` function is currently considered\0AUndefined Behavior (for any unwinding implementation):\0A\0A```rust,ignore (UB)\0A#![feature(start)]\0A\0A#[start]\0Afn start(_argc: isize, _argv: *const *const u8) -> isize {\0A    std::panic::catch_unwind(|| {\0A        panic!(); // panic safely gets caught or safely aborts execution\0A    });\0A\0A    panic!(); // UB!\0A\0A    0\0A}\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
