@anon.d1ff9934ece6813bf2a30f9ce237ed68.3189 = private unnamed_addr constant <{ [623 x i8] }> <{ [623 x i8] c"# `unboxed_closures`\0A\0AThe tracking issue for this feature is [#29625]\0A\0ASee Also: [`fn_traits`](../library-features/fn-traits.md)\0A\0A[#29625]: https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/29625\0A\0A----\0A\0AThe `unboxed_closures` feature allows you to write functions using the `\22rust-call\22` ABI,\0Arequired for implementing the [`Fn*`] family of traits. `\22rust-call\22` functions must have\0Aexactly one (non self) argument, a tuple representing the argument list.\0A\0A[`Fn*`]: ../../std/ops/trait.Fn.html\0A\0A```rust\0A#![feature(unboxed_closures)]\0A\0Aextern \22rust-call\22 fn add_args(args: (u32, u32)) -> u32 {\0A    args.0 + args.1\0A}\0A\0Afn main() {}\0A```\0A" }>, align 1
